     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Elisabeth,</div><div><br></div>ymd can only handle vector input. It looks like date is a data frame. You&#39;ll need to pass just the <span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.09090805053711px\">DurationPartner_1 column of date to ymd. </span><div>\r\n\r\n<font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\">You can extract this column as vector with</span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\">date$DurationPartner_1</span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\">and parse it with </span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\">ymd(</span></font><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.09090805053711px\">date$DurationPartner_1)</span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></font><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.09090805053711px\">Cheers,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.09090805053711px\">Garrett</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.09090805053711px\"><br></span></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">\r\n\r\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, May 8, 2014 at 2:37 AM, Elisabeth Schubach <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">elisabeth...@gmx.de</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear lubridate-users,<div><br></div><div>I am new to lubridate and tried to convert factors into dates using the following command. However, I got the following error message:</div><div><div>&gt; ymd(date)</div>\r\n\r\n<div>[1] NA.</div><div>Warning message:</div><div>All formats failed to parse. No formats found. </div><div>&gt; str(date)</div><div>&#39;data.frame&#39;:<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>1819 obs. of  1 variable:</div>\r\n\r\n<div> $ DurationPartner_1: Factor w/ 147 levels &quot;&quot;,&quot;0000-00-00&quot;,..: 104 1 1 78 131 1 135 79 68 108 ...</div></div><div><br></div><div>I would appreciate your help.</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div>Elisabeth</div></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lubridate&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lubridate+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793235797492000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1TX4C58PFYVSaR9ARJ0zLw\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
